    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n79053" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παράφρων</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάρφρων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρήν</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wandering from reason,
				senseless</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάντις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					473
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; <i>out of one's wits, deranged</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				649d
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύσσας πάρφρονος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					10.103
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί τόδ᾽ αὖ παράφρων ἔρριψας
				ἔπος</span>; <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				232
			</span></i> (anap.) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.καὶ παραπλὴξ τὴν διάνοιαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					72
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-νως, γελᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Zen.
					1.43
				</span></i>
			.</div>
